WEBVTT

00:05.967 --> 00:07.557
[wind blowing]

00:12.357 --> 00:13.397
[SITARA] What?

00:14.187 --> 00:16.987
Princess Sorghaghtani
refused the marriage after all?

00:17.067 --> 00:18.737
That's right.
Quite surprising, isn't it?

00:18.817 --> 00:20.147
So what will happen
to Lady Töregene?

00:20.237 --> 00:21.317
Her freedom depended

00:21.657 --> 00:23.237
on the princess marrying
Prince Güyük!

00:23.327 --> 00:25.367
What did Empress Boraqchin
have to say about it?

00:25.447 --> 00:28.367
Calm down, will you?
I'll tell you everything.

00:31.537 --> 00:33.497
Sorghaghtani Beki.

00:33.587 --> 00:35.957
This is what is best
for the Mongols.

00:36.047 --> 00:38.377
And it is to your benefit
as well.

00:39.087 --> 00:42.887
I must recommend that you humbly
accept our offer.

00:42.967 --> 00:44.217
♪

00:44.637 --> 00:47.217
I truly appreciate
your courtesy.

00:47.597 --> 00:50.517
However, I then remember
the wise words

00:50.597 --> 00:51.977
our great foremother,

00:52.057 --> 00:53.807
Alan Gua, said to her five sons:

00:53.897 --> 00:56.527
"A single arrow may be broken
with ease

00:56.607 --> 00:59.607
but five arrows bundled together
shan't ever be broken."

01:00.567 --> 01:01.857
Great Kha'an,

01:01.947 --> 01:05.157
Tolui was one of the arrows
bundled at your side.

01:05.237 --> 01:07.947
It falls upon me
to raise his sons.

01:08.037 --> 01:09.867
They are young
and fragile arrows

01:09.947 --> 01:11.787
still needing to be crafted.

01:13.287 --> 01:15.377
[BORAQCHIN]
The House of Tolui on its own?

01:15.917 --> 01:19.167
She refuses to be engulfed
by the House of Ögedei.

01:19.917 --> 01:21.547
[SORGHAGHTANI]
I'm quite sure your retainers

01:21.627 --> 01:23.177
-feel the same way.
-[gasps]

01:23.257 --> 01:25.007
Isn't that right, General Ilüge?

01:25.087 --> 01:26.507
Huh? Uh, yes.

01:26.597 --> 01:28.257
[SORGHAGHTANI]
You are the head retainer

01:28.347 --> 01:29.427
serving the House of Ögedei.

01:29.517 --> 01:31.137
I imagine the Great Kha'an

01:31.227 --> 01:32.887
trusts you
with his finest treasure.

01:32.977 --> 01:35.857
A sign of his
utmost confidence in you.

01:37.517 --> 01:39.147
[SITARA] His finest treasure?

01:39.227 --> 01:41.317
Does she mean Lady Töregene?

01:41.397 --> 01:42.567
Yes.

01:42.647 --> 01:44.697
She's in
General Ilüge's territory.

01:44.777 --> 01:45.947
[Ilüge groans]

01:46.027 --> 01:49.947
[♪ opening theme song playing]

03:19.327 --> 03:21.287
[ÖGEDEI]
You seem to be in a foul mood.

03:23.457 --> 03:24.587
[BORAQCHIN] Do I?

03:25.257 --> 03:27.467
Sorghaghtani sent a messenger.

03:28.047 --> 03:30.137
If it's to the
Great Kha'an's liking,

03:30.217 --> 03:32.807
she's happy
to offer up 4,000 tents

03:32.887 --> 03:34.677
from the House of Tolui.

03:34.767 --> 03:36.887
The same territory and people

03:36.977 --> 03:40.017
I had planned to deprive her of
all along.

03:40.857 --> 03:42.937
She's making a mockery of me.

03:44.687 --> 03:45.987
Are you angry at me

03:46.067 --> 03:47.897
for what I have done
to your family?

03:48.607 --> 03:50.317
[ÖGEDEI] How could I be angry?

03:50.737 --> 03:54.447
Because of you, I am finally
able to do as I wish.

03:54.827 --> 03:56.287
You have my thanks.

03:58.167 --> 04:00.287
However, I must say this,

04:00.377 --> 04:02.127
going forward,

04:02.207 --> 04:04.457
please don't involve
Töregene anymore.

04:05.007 --> 04:08.047
She is someone precious to me.
I want her protected.

04:10.547 --> 04:12.297
I understand.

04:13.717 --> 04:15.307
[SHIRA]
Prince Güyük and Sir Qadaq

04:15.387 --> 04:17.557
are heading
for General Ilüge's lands.

04:17.637 --> 04:20.137
General Ilüge served
as the Great Kha'an's tutor

04:20.227 --> 04:21.307
for many years.

04:21.607 --> 04:24.477
His influence rivals
that of the imperial family.

04:24.567 --> 04:26.567
Not even Prince Güyük
can just go there

04:26.647 --> 04:28.987
without establishing
a good reason first.

04:29.067 --> 04:31.157
Shira, we need to hurry.

04:31.567 --> 04:33.317
You'd better hold on tight then.

04:33.407 --> 04:34.777
Let's go.

04:36.407 --> 04:38.537
[SHIRA] Looks like
a rough road ahead of us.

04:38.617 --> 04:39.617
♪

04:44.587 --> 04:47.127
[SLAVE] Uh? [exclaims]

04:50.587 --> 04:52.137
Excuse me, Lady Töregene.

04:52.217 --> 04:53.507
-[slave exclaims]
-[WOMAN] Uh?

04:54.217 --> 04:55.257
[chuckles]

04:55.557 --> 04:57.967
Have you mistaken me
for that silly girl again?

04:58.057 --> 05:00.137
[slave screams] My apologies.

05:01.387 --> 05:03.897
Oh, there are way too many tents

05:03.977 --> 05:05.817
for me to remember
which is which.

05:05.897 --> 05:07.187
-[footsteps]
-Huh?

05:08.147 --> 05:09.147
[Qadaq sighs]

05:09.647 --> 05:11.197
[ILÜGE] Why,
if it isn't Prince Güyük.

05:11.277 --> 05:13.697
What brings you
to my humble abode?

05:13.777 --> 05:14.777
[GÜYÜK] Uh...

05:15.567 --> 05:18.287
Our Lady Töregene is here,
isn't she?

05:18.367 --> 05:19.787
May we speak with her?

05:19.867 --> 05:22.327
Now why would you assume
something like that?

05:23.417 --> 05:25.997
Be reasonable.
Would we have come all this way

05:26.087 --> 05:27.797
if we weren't certain?

05:27.877 --> 05:31.297
It is kind of a long story,
but let me tell you...

05:37.257 --> 05:38.427
[SHIRA] They want us to find her

05:38.507 --> 05:39.967
and make sure
that she's still safe

05:40.057 --> 05:42.267
while they try to keep
his attention elsewhere.

05:42.637 --> 05:44.137
Where would we start, even?

05:44.227 --> 05:45.437
Forget about success.

05:45.517 --> 05:47.397
If we're caught,
it could mean our heads.

05:47.477 --> 05:48.727
Hey, where are you going?

05:49.817 --> 05:52.357
-[gasps]
-[SHIRA] Hurry.

05:53.817 --> 05:55.487
[ELJIGIDEI]
This could be dangerous.

05:55.567 --> 05:57.407
We must do everything we can

05:57.487 --> 05:59.737
to conceal the fact that
Lady Töregene is here.

05:59.827 --> 06:00.947
[Sitara gasps]

06:01.037 --> 06:02.157
[ARGHUN] Hm?

06:02.907 --> 06:03.787
Uh?

06:03.867 --> 06:06.497
[dog whines]

06:06.577 --> 06:08.917
[ELJIGIDEI]
What's wrong? Let's go.

06:08.997 --> 06:10.087
[ARGHUN] Right.

06:10.547 --> 06:12.547
[ELJIGIDEI]
And how is Lady Töregene faring?

06:12.627 --> 06:14.587
[ARGHUN]
I went to see her just earlier.

06:14.677 --> 06:15.887
She's doing well.

06:17.297 --> 06:19.757
[sighs] Did you hear
what they said?

06:19.847 --> 06:21.847
That means we've confirmed
that she's safe,

06:21.927 --> 06:23.637
and we can head back for now--
[grunts]

06:23.727 --> 06:25.387
Hey, wait! Ah!

06:30.317 --> 06:31.737
[cloth rustles]

06:32.187 --> 06:33.447
[footsteps]

06:33.527 --> 06:35.777
Lady Töregene,
I thank you for waiting.

06:35.857 --> 06:37.067
I've brought your meal.

06:37.487 --> 06:39.527
[sighs] You're late.

06:39.617 --> 06:41.747
[SLAVE] My deepest apologies.

06:41.827 --> 06:43.367
I got lost again.

06:43.447 --> 06:44.457
[Töregene sighs]

06:49.497 --> 06:50.877
Why is there no urum?

06:50.957 --> 06:53.167
Hm? Urum's been out of season

06:53.257 --> 06:55.047
for quite some time now,
my lady.

06:55.377 --> 06:58.137
I was just asking.
Now, leave me.

06:58.217 --> 06:59.717
Uh! Of course!

07:10.437 --> 07:11.477
[exclaims]

07:13.567 --> 07:15.107
Oh, Fatima.

07:16.237 --> 07:17.487
[SITARA] Lady Töregene.

07:18.067 --> 07:19.737
Lady Töregene.

07:20.527 --> 07:22.617
-Lady Töregene.
-[SHIRA] Hey, stop!

07:22.697 --> 07:24.327
-We need to head back!
-[gasps]

07:25.367 --> 07:28.207
[SLAVE] Lady Töregene
is so hard to please.

07:28.287 --> 07:29.627
[Sitara gasps]

07:29.707 --> 07:31.087
♪

07:46.427 --> 07:47.557
[gasps softly]

07:49.017 --> 07:50.107
[TÖREGENE] Hm?

07:50.437 --> 07:52.477
[exclaims] Lady Töregene!

07:52.567 --> 07:56.147
Fatima? What are you doing here?

07:56.237 --> 07:58.567
Thank goodness.
You're really all right!

07:58.647 --> 08:00.487
I finally get to see you again.

08:00.567 --> 08:01.567
[Töregene gasps softly]

08:02.027 --> 08:03.157
♪

08:04.327 --> 08:06.117
I don't understand.

08:06.197 --> 08:08.207
Even though I betrayed you...

08:11.287 --> 08:13.627
[SITARA] Lady Töregene, look.

08:14.457 --> 08:17.667
Despite everything,
you managed to protect them.

08:18.217 --> 08:19.757
All the feelings...

08:20.677 --> 08:23.047
that are the most precious
to me.

08:23.967 --> 08:25.097
No.

08:26.057 --> 08:28.017
The most precious to us.

08:32.727 --> 08:35.017
[TÖREGENE]
The Great Khatun told me this:

08:36.357 --> 08:40.197
In my previous days,
I waited upon Empress Khulan.

08:40.737 --> 08:42.617
[Töregene gasps] Khulan?

08:43.317 --> 08:46.117
The one who taught me
how to find the joys in life.

08:46.447 --> 08:48.577
And who offered herself
to the Mongols

08:48.657 --> 08:51.037
to protect the Merkits
facing ruin.

08:51.117 --> 08:52.287
Khulan.

08:53.747 --> 08:55.167
[BORAQCHIN] I always had a sense

08:55.247 --> 08:57.707
that she bore
feelings of resentment.

08:57.797 --> 08:59.837
It seems that even to this day,

08:59.917 --> 09:02.387
you harbor those same feelings
toward the Mongols.

09:02.467 --> 09:04.177
Did she really?

09:05.887 --> 09:08.927
Please allow me
to lend you my assistance.

09:10.557 --> 09:12.687
So that you may be
able to achieve

09:12.767 --> 09:14.147
what she wished she could.

09:15.647 --> 09:18.527
[TÖREGENE] I thought my chance
to kill Ögedei had come.

09:19.067 --> 09:23.157
The Great Khatun told me
that you were not to be trusted.

09:23.237 --> 09:24.697
[Sitara gasps]

09:24.777 --> 09:26.197
I was a fool.

09:27.407 --> 09:30.037
[exclaims] I fell for her lies,

09:30.117 --> 09:32.787
and betrayed
both you and Khulan.

09:33.247 --> 09:34.537
♪

09:36.707 --> 09:38.297
[SITARA] Lady Töregene...

09:39.087 --> 09:42.297
I, too, found myself confronted.

09:44.047 --> 09:46.177
With the thought
of abandoning the past

09:46.257 --> 09:48.007
and moving on with my life...

09:50.477 --> 09:53.307
I ended up betraying
you as well.

09:55.187 --> 09:57.977
Fatima sure
is taking her time talking.

09:58.067 --> 10:00.647
We need to get going
before we're discovered.

10:00.937 --> 10:02.317
[gasps]

10:02.397 --> 10:04.527
Wait, is that really
who I think it is?

10:04.607 --> 10:05.657
Uh, no way.

10:05.737 --> 10:07.737
Sorry, but you're
on your own now.

10:07.827 --> 10:09.277
[running footsteps]

10:09.367 --> 10:11.037
[footsteps]

10:14.957 --> 10:16.707
-[cloth rustles]
-[ÖGEDEI] I'm coming in.

10:16.787 --> 10:17.747
[BOTH] Uh?

10:17.837 --> 10:19.127
[gasps]

10:19.587 --> 10:21.377
[SITARA] Great Kha'an!

10:24.677 --> 10:26.467
And what is it you want?

10:26.547 --> 10:29.967
If my fate is to be executed,
then let us be done with it.

10:30.057 --> 10:33.137
Of course not.
I have a favor to ask of you.

10:33.227 --> 10:34.307
[TÖREGENE] Hm?

10:34.807 --> 10:36.137
You may enter.

10:38.307 --> 10:40.227
-[Töregene gasps]
-Hello, Mother.

10:40.897 --> 10:42.277
My darling Güyük!

10:42.357 --> 10:43.357
[SITARA] "My darling Güyük?"

10:43.437 --> 10:45.447
Oh, my goodness,
what are you doing here,

10:45.527 --> 10:46.567
my little darling?

10:46.657 --> 10:48.157
Is my little boy all right?

10:48.237 --> 10:50.117
You didn't run
into anything scary, did you?

10:50.197 --> 10:52.447
I'm quite well, Mother.
Please try to calm yourself.

10:52.537 --> 10:53.537
[Töregene sighs]

10:54.617 --> 10:58.587
I beg of you, Mother, come back
with me to my territory.

10:59.537 --> 11:00.497
[TÖREGENE] Huh?

11:00.587 --> 11:02.087
It lies to the west,

11:02.167 --> 11:05.007
on the steppe between the
Altai Mountains and Tian Shan.

11:05.967 --> 11:08.967
The winters are cold,
but there's plenty of water.

11:09.047 --> 11:11.007
And the pastures are lush.

11:11.097 --> 11:12.637
And what's more,

11:13.387 --> 11:14.927
it is far away from here.

11:15.017 --> 11:16.137
[Töregene gasps]

11:16.637 --> 11:17.637
[Sitara gasps softly]

11:17.727 --> 11:19.057
♪

11:19.147 --> 11:21.857
I ask the same, Töregene.

11:22.607 --> 11:26.527
The court is much too tumultuous
a place for you and Güyük, no?

11:27.527 --> 11:31.327
If you will agree to go,
I won't ask any more of you.

11:33.537 --> 11:36.327
All I want
is for you to be happy.

11:39.037 --> 11:40.337
[SITARA] I see.

11:40.417 --> 11:42.747
That would certainly resolve
everything tidily.

11:43.957 --> 11:46.087
Empress Boraqchin wanted
Prince Güyük

11:46.167 --> 11:48.507
and Princess Sorghaghtani
to get married

11:48.587 --> 11:51.257
as a condition
for Lady Töregene's freedom.

11:51.757 --> 11:53.757
Her aim was to remove
the three of them

11:53.847 --> 11:55.517
from the imperial court.

11:56.677 --> 11:59.647
That particular scheme of hers
didn't bear fruit, though.

12:00.857 --> 12:02.977
But with this plan,
all three of them

12:03.067 --> 12:05.687
will leave the political stage
still the same.

12:07.027 --> 12:10.277
And it isn't a terrible proposal
for Lady Töregene, either.

12:18.367 --> 12:19.667
[GÜYÜK] All right then, Mother.

12:20.497 --> 12:23.417
Tomorrow, I'll come fetch you.

12:25.627 --> 12:27.837
Sorry for such a commotion.

12:27.917 --> 12:29.507
[ILÜGE] Will that be all?

12:29.587 --> 12:30.637
[ÖGEDEI] Yes.

12:31.547 --> 12:33.927
-But before I go...
-[ILÜGE] Oh?

12:35.007 --> 12:36.387
[ÖGEDEI] Töregene...

12:36.467 --> 12:39.937
If I may, can I speak
with your lady-in-waiting?

12:40.017 --> 12:41.017
[TÖREGENE] Huh?

12:41.097 --> 12:42.107
[SITARA] Huh?

12:42.187 --> 12:43.357
Oh.

12:45.727 --> 12:47.857
Why do you wanna talk to me?

12:47.937 --> 12:49.947
So you're Fatima, correct?

12:50.027 --> 12:52.947
Möge spoke of you.
I hear you get lost easily.

12:53.027 --> 12:55.367
Uh...
[chuckles nervously]

12:55.447 --> 12:58.787
And I've also heard that
you're a scholar's daughter.

12:58.867 --> 13:00.537
Are you knowledgeable
in the stars?

13:00.617 --> 13:01.957
The stars?

13:02.037 --> 13:03.537
[ILÜGE] Please, Great Kha'an!

13:03.627 --> 13:05.287
You really
mustn't speak directly

13:05.377 --> 13:07.257
to someone so far beneath you!

13:07.337 --> 13:08.417
[ÖGEDEI] Hmm.

13:08.507 --> 13:10.797
Allow my son
to relay the words for you.

13:10.877 --> 13:12.337
-Go!
-Oh, all right.

13:13.797 --> 13:15.347
[ELJIGIDEI] The emperor asks,

13:15.427 --> 13:17.007
"Are you knowledgeable
in the stars?"

13:17.097 --> 13:20.177
Why, yes. I am. Considerably so.

13:21.807 --> 13:24.687
"Why, yes, I am.
Considerably so." Sire!

13:24.767 --> 13:26.977
Good. Would she happen to know

13:27.067 --> 13:29.147
why the stars move across
the night sky?

13:29.237 --> 13:30.237
[ELJIGIDEI] Oh.

13:31.067 --> 13:32.607
[ELJIGIDEI] "Good.
Would she happen to know

13:32.697 --> 13:34.367
why the stars move
across the night sky?"

13:34.447 --> 13:36.027
The Great Kha'an asks.

13:36.117 --> 13:37.487
Um...

13:37.947 --> 13:39.867
Well, that much I do know.

13:39.947 --> 13:42.407
I read it in a book
by Al-Biruni.

13:44.667 --> 13:45.957
♪

13:46.037 --> 13:48.587
"He created the sun, moon,
and the stars.

13:48.667 --> 13:50.797
All are subject to His command."

13:50.877 --> 13:53.047
So it is written in the Quran.

13:53.587 --> 13:55.597
This means that
the movement of the stars

13:55.677 --> 13:58.057
is a blessing
granted to us by Allah.

13:59.387 --> 14:02.557
Furthermore, the heavens
are eight layers of spheres

14:02.637 --> 14:04.097
revolving in place.

14:04.187 --> 14:07.057
And we reside in the center
of those spheres.

14:08.687 --> 14:11.187
-Hmm.
-[ELJIGIDEI] That's a lot.

14:11.277 --> 14:13.237
[ÖGEDEI] Oh? How amusing.

14:13.317 --> 14:15.817
-[Eljigidei gasps]
-Did you say amusing?

14:15.907 --> 14:17.367
Hey, you don't talk to him!

14:17.447 --> 14:20.287
Yes. Quite different
from what I know.

14:20.617 --> 14:23.997
When I was younger, I was told
that in the night sky,

14:24.077 --> 14:27.207
the stars are livestock
tied to a pillar in heaven.

14:27.287 --> 14:29.537
That pillar is the star
in the north sky

14:29.627 --> 14:31.007
that never moves.

14:31.547 --> 14:32.917
With all due respect,

14:33.007 --> 14:35.007
-that is merely a superstition.
-[gasps]

14:35.087 --> 14:36.177
[ÖGEDEI] You think so?

14:36.797 --> 14:39.137
For all that we know
and don't know,

14:39.217 --> 14:41.347
our world could be
a galloping horse

14:41.427 --> 14:42.557
bound to a rope.

14:42.637 --> 14:44.347
Riding that horse...

14:44.427 --> 14:45.977
myself and Boraqchin.

14:46.057 --> 14:47.807
Sorghaghtani and Tolui.

14:47.897 --> 14:49.607
And of course, you and Töregene.

14:49.687 --> 14:51.267
All of us on its back,

14:51.357 --> 14:54.437
circling as we head toward
the same destination.

14:54.527 --> 14:55.647
Utter nonsense.

14:55.737 --> 14:57.867
It's against the very concept
of science.

14:58.907 --> 15:00.907
-Science, you say?
-[Eljigidei gasps]

15:00.987 --> 15:01.907
[Sitara sighs]

15:02.247 --> 15:05.457
Yes, science.
The laws that govern nature.

15:06.077 --> 15:07.377
The work of Allah,

15:07.457 --> 15:09.877
who created the world
and bestowed it to us.

15:10.247 --> 15:13.167
Science is the discipline
that seeks to study this.

15:14.797 --> 15:16.507
Well, in that case,

15:16.587 --> 15:18.757
there are spirits
that the kams speak of.

15:18.847 --> 15:21.887
I'd say their existence explains
the laws of nature well enough.

15:21.967 --> 15:23.177
You're wrong.

15:23.267 --> 15:25.477
The Quran tells us
that Allah made the stars

15:25.557 --> 15:28.397
move across the sky
to help give us direction.

15:28.477 --> 15:30.897
The positions and paths
of the stars are calculated

15:30.977 --> 15:32.187
with Earth at its center,

15:32.267 --> 15:34.937
giving us results
without any contradiction.

15:35.027 --> 15:36.397
What more proof
could you possibly need

15:36.487 --> 15:37.947
to see that this is the truth?

15:38.027 --> 15:40.317
Anything else is a mere figment!

15:40.407 --> 15:42.197
[breathes heavily]

15:44.867 --> 15:46.327
[wind blows]

15:47.287 --> 15:48.247
[Ögedei chuckles]

15:48.327 --> 15:49.417
I see now.

15:49.917 --> 15:52.957
You must get along
very well with Töregene.

15:53.377 --> 15:55.837
What if you and I made a wager?

15:56.547 --> 15:58.087
A wager?

15:58.177 --> 16:01.507
[ÖGEDEI] Yes. But one where
all you have to do is watch.

16:03.347 --> 16:04.717
In the days ahead,

16:04.807 --> 16:07.427
I will bring prosperity
to the Mongol Empire.

16:07.517 --> 16:10.897
With methods unlike those
of my father or Tolui.

16:12.017 --> 16:15.317
So that you and Töregene
can find happiness.

16:15.397 --> 16:17.027
Find happiness?

16:17.567 --> 16:18.947
[ÖGEDEI] That's right.

16:19.447 --> 16:21.737
When I first
laid eyes upon Töregene,

16:21.817 --> 16:23.987
I realized what my duty is.

16:24.987 --> 16:27.827
I must create
the Mongol Empire anew...

16:28.327 --> 16:31.827
Solely because of the look
in her eyes.

16:32.707 --> 16:35.917
You've lost your homeland
and family as well, no?

16:37.007 --> 16:38.417
Your eyes earlier,

16:38.507 --> 16:41.427
they were the very image
of hers on that day.

16:44.467 --> 16:47.887
So watch me with those
very same eyes of yours.

16:48.887 --> 16:51.647
If you two manage
to find happiness here,

16:52.687 --> 16:54.267
victory is mine.

16:54.357 --> 16:55.517
♪

17:25.177 --> 17:27.387
[breathing heavily]

17:29.597 --> 17:31.847
[grunting]

17:31.937 --> 17:35.147
[screaming]

17:35.727 --> 17:36.687
[thuds]

17:37.977 --> 17:39.777
[panting]

17:39.857 --> 17:41.737
[wind blowing]

17:49.367 --> 17:51.537
[bleating]

18:07.217 --> 18:08.137
[TÖREGENE] Fatima?

18:08.217 --> 18:09.597
[Sitara gasps]

18:09.677 --> 18:12.477
-Fatima.
-Oh, Lady Töregene!

18:12.557 --> 18:14.267
Are you all right?

18:14.727 --> 18:18.067
Uh, yes. But how are you doing?

18:19.857 --> 18:21.817
You know, Fatima...

18:22.647 --> 18:24.697
I've been thinking
more about it.

18:32.787 --> 18:36.127
I think I won't be going
to live with my Güyük.

18:36.207 --> 18:37.337
[Sitara gasps]

18:37.417 --> 18:39.587
Why, doing that would be

18:39.667 --> 18:41.957
just what
the Great Kha'an wants.

18:42.457 --> 18:45.127
And the very thought of it
infuriates me.

18:45.217 --> 18:46.757
[Sitara gasps]

18:47.637 --> 18:50.507
Fatima, will you...

18:52.017 --> 18:54.927
Will you fight by my side
once more?

18:55.017 --> 18:55.977
♪

18:56.057 --> 18:57.307
[Sitara breathes softly]

18:58.767 --> 19:00.067
The thing is...

19:01.727 --> 19:05.107
I'm not clever,
not even a little bit, you know?

19:05.817 --> 19:07.067
♪

19:16.367 --> 19:17.457
[Sitara gasps]

19:19.087 --> 19:22.707
Let the two of us
summon a storm upon them.

19:23.757 --> 19:24.917
[SITARA] That's right.

19:25.587 --> 19:28.217
I'm not fighting
the Great Kha'an by myself.

19:28.297 --> 19:30.137
I'm not alone anymore.

19:31.387 --> 19:32.887
This empire...

19:33.427 --> 19:36.847
And the Mongols who chose to
take everything we had from us.

19:37.517 --> 19:40.397
We can never allow them
to be thought of as good.

19:42.647 --> 19:45.107
Fatima, now it's our turn.

19:49.117 --> 19:50.907
To become the witches.

19:52.737 --> 19:55.577
[♪ closing theme song playing]

21:22.917 --> 21:24.627
[wind howling]

21:26.747 --> 21:29.007
[SITARA (ADULT)] That year,
the winter came

21:29.087 --> 21:31.047
as it always does.

21:31.127 --> 21:34.847
And eventually,
so, too, did the summer.

21:35.847 --> 21:39.387
On the steppe, the grass sprouts
anew once more,

21:40.057 --> 21:43.647
and the sheep graze peacefully
upon the soft buds.

21:43.727 --> 21:44.727
♪

22:08.837 --> 22:11.967
Everything perfectly unchanging.

22:13.047 --> 22:16.047
The steppe, same as ever.

22:20.717 --> 22:22.677
But is it really?

22:23.387 --> 22:25.557
[TÖREGENE]
Good day to you, Great Khatun.

22:25.937 --> 22:28.067
Fine weather we're having.

22:28.607 --> 22:30.107
[SITARA]
It's as though it embodies

22:30.187 --> 22:32.687
the growing prosperity
of the empire.

22:34.027 --> 22:36.447
Yes, I would agree.

22:37.197 --> 22:39.577
Second Empress Töregene,

22:40.947 --> 22:42.657
and her lady-in-waiting,

22:43.247 --> 22:44.747
Fatima.

22:45.787 --> 22:47.167
[Sitara chuckles]

22:47.247 --> 22:48.627
♪

22:52.047 --> 22:54.797
[SITARA (ADULT)] That year,
Emperor Ögedei

22:54.877 --> 22:57.507
appointed a governor
to oversee Persia.

22:58.347 --> 23:01.307
And the land that Sitara
once called home

23:01.387 --> 23:03.677
finally fell under
the permanent rule

23:03.767 --> 23:05.637
of the Mongol Empire.

23:06.347 --> 23:07.557
However...

23:07.977 --> 23:10.897
the dispute that this position
would cause...

23:10.977 --> 23:14.397
eventually, would turn into
a great storm

23:14.487 --> 23:17.447
that would shake
the empire to its core.

23:18.157 --> 23:21.537
But no one knew this yet.
